// How each generic setter class of the .ork loader reads the text of an element: the texts go
// through the entries of the setter table (DocumentConfig) that OpenRocket registers with that
// class, and warnings and values have to be OpenRocket's (see SetterTestSupport.h for the probe;
// the rows are written by its scripts/make_tests.py).
//
// A row whose comment starts with "OpenRocket:" is a deliberate deviation: the comment gives
// OpenRocket's answer and the reason, the row QtRocket's.

